nct IDs in 3 of 3 runs.\n  - The test that guarded this (test_new.sh N=10) was moved onto a store with claims, so the suite no longer sees it.\n  - The ticket records retiring the loop as a decision (line 169, \"residual race\"). The measurement contradicts \"residual\", and the help's \"keeps the old residual race\" is wrong: main did not have this race.\n  - Fix: keep the glob post-check on the claims-off path only, or have the author confirm the trade-off and reword the help and manual to say such stores now collide on any same-checkout race.\n- Exit criteria 1-9: met by the diff and tests. Criterion 10 (make check): CI passing on the head, targeted suites pass.\n- Never-lose-data on the new write paths holds:\n  - temp+link publication, with EEXIST as the collision signal and no clobber;\n  - the ticket is created with O_EXCL and `.keep` with O_EXCL;\n  - a symlinked `.claims` is refused through Lstat;\n  - writes stay under `<store>/.claims`, and no ticket file is rewritten or removed.\n- redteam, raised as blocking and downgraded to consider: when hard links are unsupported, the fallback create can leave a partial claim if erg is killed (src/go/claims.go:149-153). Hitting it needs both a filesystem without hard links and a kill inside a write of about 40 bytes. Only the marker is affected, `erg check` flags it, and the code comment documents it. No real-user scenario clears the bar.\n- redteam, consider: check and migrate follow a symlinked individual claim file (src/go/claims.go:219-224). No real actor makes one, and src/go/atomicwrite.go:49-52 declares symlink hardening a non-goal. A write onto it fails with EEXIST, so nothing is written outside the store.\n- correctness, consider:\n  - The criterion-8 unit race test is sequential, through the allocateID seam (claims_test.go:159). The N=10 concurrent shell test covers the real race.\n  - The hook is hardcoded to `tickets/.claims`.\n  - The ignore probe checks only `.claims/0001` (claims.go:96).\n- consider (